Given a slice, compute the number of indices it spans, i.e. the
number of iterations that for_range_slice() will execute.

Pseudo-code:
    assert step != 0
    if step > 0:
        if stop <= start:
            return 0
        else:
            return (stop - start - 1) // step + 1
    else:
        if stop >= start:
            return 0
        else:
            return (stop - start + 1) // step + 1

(see PySlice_GetIndicesEx() in CPython)

